"""R83 = R57 gate (same decision, cheaper): see gate83.py for the exact-decision fast path and its error bound; production no longer logs the 512 logits (R83_LOG_LOGITS=1 enables it for gate runs).
R57 = R54 rule plus a confidence-gated C(1) (gate83.py): after each draft a deterministic confidence of the 512 exact candidate logits is compared with GATE_TAU; below it the cycle runs the EOS-C1 machinery (mode GATE-C1) instead of M2.
GATE_TAU=None disables the gate (logging only; used by the calibration run). The deployed values are the pre-declared calibration selection (ROUND55.md): top1_prob, tau 0.4. Verification is unchanged, outputs are token-identical.
R54 fixed rule: switch at the first token boundary that observes CPU prime completion AND whose last committed token is not a sentence-final token.
Verification is unchanged, so the rule only moves work between exact serial rows and exact M2 cycles; it never changes any output token.
Rationale (R51/R83 measured components): entering speculation costs a drafter catch-up (~3 ms) plus a first proposal (~3.5 ms) before any row runs, and
an EOS proposal then runs the same C(1) row a serial row would run (verify 19.21 vs serial 19.25 ms), so a request that ends right after a finished
sentence pays ~7 ms for nothing. A sentence-final token is the position where EOS is most likely, so the controller runs one more exact serial row there.
SENTENCE_FINAL_IDS: every vocabulary piece (107520 ids) whose bytes end with U+3002, U+FF01, U+FF1F, '.', '!' or '?'; re-derived from the tokenizer by the sentence-final gate."""
